<!--
	A character reference naming an entity of two code points: the HTML5 table gives
	both, Svelte's generated table carries one per name, so the second is dropped.
-->
<p>combining mark: &NotEqualTilde; &nLt; &acE;</p>
<p>variation selector: &caps;</p>
<p>two characters: &fjlig; &ThickSpace;</p>
<div data-attr="&bne;"></div>

<!-- The base characters each pairs with, where the two decoders agree -->
<p>base character: &esim; &ll; &ac; &cap;</p>
<div data-attr="&equals;"></div>
